  <p>Wholesale gym wear in the UK is driven by speed, style, fit, and repeatability. A buyer may be a boutique fitness studio, an online DTC brand, a small wholesale distributor, or a creator-led label. The sourcing goal is the same: launch products quickly, protect margin, and avoid quality issues that create returns.</p>

  <h2>What UK Wholesale Buyers Need</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Reliable bestsellers such as leggings, sports bras, shorts, oversized tees, hoodies, and matching sets.</li>
    <li>Flexible MOQ for testing colors, sizes, and product categories.</li>
    <li>Good compression, squat-proof fabric, and stable stitching.</li>
    <li>Private label branding without long development cycles.</li>
    <li>Clear production and shipping communication.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Build a Smarter First Order</h2>
  <p>For UK wholesale buyers, a focused first order usually performs better than a wide but shallow collection. Start with two or three hero products, choose commercial colors, and keep sizing practical. Use customer feedback to guide the second order.</p>

  <h2>Recommended Launch Mix</h2>
  <div class="market-table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Product</th><th>Why It Works</th><th>Private Label Option</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Squat-proof leggings</td><td>Core UK activewear bestseller</td><td>Waistband logo, woven label, hangtag</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sports bras</td><td>Pairs with leggings for higher order value</td><td>Chest logo, size label, packaging</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Oversized tees</td><td>Strong gym and lifestyle crossover</td><td>Screen print, embroidery, neck label</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Quality Questions Before You Buy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Can you show fabric stretch and opacity testing?</li>
    <li>What stitching is used for leggings and sports bras?</li>
    <li>Can you provide measurements for each size?</li>
    <li>How are defects handled before shipment?</li>
    <li>Can you support repeat orders in the same fabric and color?</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Fitclo's Recommendation for UK Buyers</h2>
  <p>Start with wholesale-ready private label styles if you need speed and lower risk. Move into custom manufacturing once you know which silhouettes, colors, and fabric weights are working for your UK customers.</p>
